From a50037b9601e956b5c1f6028125405e70069547a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:43:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Give the Sound Blaster ring its own pages, take IRQ 2 as
 9, keep the mixer index

- The ring buffer is allocated on 4 KB boundaries in whole pages
  (SDL_aligned_alloc) and locked/unlocked with that rounded size. The DPMI
  host keeps one lock bit per page, so unlocking a ring that shared a page with
  another locked allocation (a thread stack) would have unlocked that too.
  The other lock pairs: statics are locked and never unlocked, DMA buffers are
  conventional memory.
- BLASTER I2 is the slave cascade: it is taken as IRQ 9 (DOS_HookInterrupt
  unmasks both PIC lines) instead of being ignored.
- The handler's read of the SB16 interrupt status (mixer register 0x82) saves
  and restores the mixer index port, so a main-thread mixer access interrupted
  between its index and data writes does not hit register 0x82.
- DOS_SBGetStats restores the caller's IF instead of executing sti; the
  interrupt counter is reset when a device opens.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
